# [PLANTS](../wg/plants.html)

## Summary

The PLANTS Working Group met at IETF 127 to discuss progress on core Merkle Tree Certificates (MTC) specifications, deployment use cases, landmark distribution, revocation models, and MTC architecture. The core document `draft-ietf-plants-merkle-tree-certs` is nearing completion with stable OIDs assigned and target deployments planned for 2027. The newly adopted deployment use cases draft (`draft-ietf-plants-mtc-deploy-use-cases`) has been streamlined, splitting technical mechanisms like Landmark Distribution Points (LDP) into `draft-gray-plants-mtc-ldp`. The working group also reviewed proposals for MTC revocation mechanisms and discussed a new formal guarantees-based MTC architecture draft (`draft-kanjalkar-plants-mtc-arch`).

