### MTC Deployment Use Cases & Landmark Distribution Point (LDP)
- **Presenter**: John Gray
- **Slides**: [MTC Deployment Use Cases updates with slides for draft-gray-plants-mtc-ldp](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-plants-mtc-deployment-use-cases-updates-with-slides-for-draft-gray-plants-mtc-ldp-00)
- **Drafts**: `draft-ietf-plants-mtc-deploy-use-cases`, `draft-gray-plants-mtc-ldp`

- **Use Cases Update (`draft-ietf-plants-mtc-deploy-use-cases`)**:
  - The document was adopted and expanded with a section titled "To MTC or not to MTC" evaluating trade-offs.
  - Detailed technical mechanisms were pruned from the high-level use cases draft into separate standalone drafts, including the LDP mechanism. Additional use cases (e.g., IKEv2, firmware batch signing) are under consideration.

- **Landmark Distribution Point (`draft-gray-plants-mtc-ldp`)**:
  - Introduces an X.509 extension and query/response format to fetch landmark subtrees and co-signatures for non-Web PKI / private PKI environments that do not utilize public transparency logs.
  - Future revisions (v01) will detail LDP operator requirements, asynchronous landmark fetching, advertisement of landmark update frequencies, media types, and error structures.

- **Discussion**:
  - **Private PKI Justification**: Panos Kampanakis requested that the use cases draft provide concrete, specific justifications for where MTCs provide clear value over traditional X.509 in private PKIs.
  - **Security Concerns**: Andrei Popov and Dennis Jackson pointed out security risks regarding fetching URLs provided in unauthenticated certificates (isomorphic to AIA issues). John Gray noted that authenticated channels, local policy, or protocols like EST will be specified to address this.

